comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-21T11:20:09.951Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence 2026-11-21: GitHub withdrew GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf on 2026-11-18T15:38:56Z (gh api /advisories/GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf reports withdrawn_at; first_patched_version is still null, picomatch is still 4.0.7). On main 06326bcf2, node scripts/release/dependency-advisories/gate.mjs passed over 552 packages with waived [] and unused_waivers ['GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf in picomatch'], so neither the registry feed nor OSV reports picomatch any more. On branch fix/history-remedies-converge the waiver registry keeps version 1 and its 3-day notice window with an empty waivers list, the mirrored .trivyignore entry CVE-2026-112366 is gone, and docs/DEVELOPMENT_DEPENDENCY_SECURITY.md records the withdrawal. After the change the gate passes with no waivers, defect-evidence-gate.mjs --waiver-notice passes (live dependency advisory waivers 0), and the dependency-advisories and defect-evidence-gate specs pass (126 tests). The built-in linear-time glob matcher from pm-gh1748 stays."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T21:32:17.484Z","harness:claude-code","Owner decision 2026-11-17: admin-merge PR 1746 despite the environmental advisory failure, and add a time-bounded waiver so the daily release continues while upstream has no patch. Design (this PR): config/dependency-advisory-waivers.json declares exact waivers (GitHub advisory id + npm package + exact locked versions + pm owner + reason >= 20 chars + RFC 3339 UTC expiry at most 30 days past the judging run; notice window 0 to 30 days). scripts/release/dependency-advisories/waivers.mjs validates them with no dist import (the gate runs before pnpm build in quality:static). Receipt version 2 records each registry advisory's validated package, severity, GitHub id and finding versions; a malformed detail voids the advisory's waivability. verifyReceipt checks counts, ids and advisory list agree, then covers each OSV row id and each registry finding version only by an exact live waiver; the verdict discloses waived and unused_waivers. Any malformed, duplicate, expired or over-long waiver refuses even when unused. The gate's refusal now names the uncovered package@version advisory (validated fields only) instead of the generic message. defect-evidence-gate --waiver-notice gained a dependency_advisory check: same validity rules, the declared notice window through the SDK waiverNoticeFor primitive, and an owner that must be an open tracker item; its negative control seeds an advisory waiver an hour from expiry."
  "2026-11-17T22:39:29.038Z","harness:claude-code","Runtime side: pm-gh1748 removed tinyglobby (and so fdir and picomatch) from the published runtime graph, so consumers' production audits are clean; picomatch remains only in development tooling. The waiver mechanism is tracked by child pm-3mdmtd; this item stays open as the waiver's owner until a patched picomatch is in the lockfile and the waiver is deleted (the scheduled notice gate fails if this item closes while the waiver exists)."
  "2026-11-18T01:56:29.888Z","harness:claude-code","The required Trivy job flags the same advisory under its CVE alias CVE-2026-112366. .trivyignore now carries 'CVE-2026-112366 exp:2026-12-01', with a comment naming this item and GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf. A unit test (waivers.spec.ts) keeps every .trivyignore entry time-bounded, mirroring a declared waiver, and expiring no later than it. Verified locally with Trivy: exit 0 with the entry, exit 1 without it. When the patched picomatch lands, delete the waiver and the .trivyignore entry together."
  "2026-11-18T02:55:38.986Z","harness:claude-code","OpenSSF Scorecard code-scanning alert 29 (rule VulnerabilitiesID, high) now cites GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf through the development graph. It is the same advisory and is left open deliberately: the vulnerability is real, and Scorecard re-raises the alert on its next run, so dismissing it would only hide state. It clears when the patched picomatch lands, together with the waiver and the .trivyignore entry."
